{
  "app": "Jira Cloud",
  "fake_bot_id": "Jira",
  "notes": "Jira Cloud for Slack issue notifications, matched to the REAL Slack app layout (verified against a live Jira Cloud message 2026-08). Fidelity rules: (1) the title is a bold mrkdwn LINK to the issue (`*<url|KEY-# Summary>*`) in a `section` \u2014 NOT a `header` block; (2) fields are inline in one mrkdwn line with small icons and bold values \u2014 `*Status:* In Progress  *Type:* Task  *Assignee:* <name>` then `*Priority:* Medium` \u2014 an \u2191/\u2193 arrow marks priority; (3) an `actions` row of real buttons \u2014 Assign, Change status, \u2728 AI Summarise \u2014 plus a trailing `static_select` placeholder 'More actions...'; (4) a small `context` footer 'Added by Jira Cloud'. Post as the Jira Cloud app via chat:write.customize with icon_url = <LOGO_BASE>/jira_cloud.png. UNFURL: to also unfurl the REAL work item beneath the card, pass send_app_notification.py --ticket-url <https://<site>.atlassian.net/browse/KEY-#>; the helper retargets the title link at that url, appends the BARE url to the message text (Slack only unfurls bare urls in `text`, never `<url|label>` links inside blocks), and sets unfurl_links=True. The real unfurl only renders if the Jira Cloud Slack app is installed in the target org and connected to that atlassian site. The `demo_real_unfurl` example below already points at a real ticket in the jenniferhynes.atlassian.net demo site.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "name": "issue_created",
